            "notes": "Round 2: Hold on to your greens, they have the best stat-per-dollar ratio of the items, and this build doesn't need any of the specialized secondary effects of the blues and purples as much as simple stats.\n\nAs a general rule of thumb, I prioritize damage with this build over defense. This is because lifesteal is such an important facet of it, and lifesteal is only effective if you are outputting a lot of DPS. Also, the lifesteal blue that's unique to Winston,  [Current Convertor](item_4a92d2ed-ed38-4c72-a55a-590e5962cecd), is not as good as the generic lifesteal blue,  [Technoleech](item_cb7fd8bf-bdcc-439a-ad35-372f24a027a8), because you will be using the primary fire much more in this build and the extra stats from [Technoleech](item_cb7fd8bf-bdcc-439a-ad35-372f24a027a8) are much more useful. [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f) can replace [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) if you are short on cash, or sell [Ammo Reserves](item_982d53aa-5ef4-493f-93e7-9e374d0ebf34) (least important green item). \n\nIf you're really struggling to stay alive and desire some defense (maybe matched up against Reaper or Junker Queen), grab [Crusader Hydraulics](item_b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09) in the Survival blues for a bit more tankiness coupled with a little attack speed as a bonus. I prefer it over [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) because Winston already has a good amount of base Armor and you should be diving at full health and retreating at half or a third health anyway.",
