            "notes": "Round 5: At this point I will often pick up [Tesla Field](item_68f73d99-6d07-40f5-ad28-0c69f45487c7) for my power for some extra offense. I'm usually dropping my shield on top of the enemy team when I jump on them, so the damage, and the lifesteal from it thanks to [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643), is more useful than [Surge Protector](item_5a653c7a-e156-449c-905b-83a1a54e7f93)'s overhealth to my teammates. [Pocket Projector](item_5c95fa4f-6f53-494e-9b4a-a7e2766cb1e8) is cool in theory but the 5% sized shield is pretty wimpy in my opinion and not worth it. \n\nTo combo with [Tesla Field](item_68f73d99-6d07-40f5-ad28-0c69f45487c7) I grab [Simian Supplements](item_7e9a42b8-2aed-4932-bba4-8ac0925ae355) (the funniest Winston item name to me) to make the shield last longer and therefore deal more damage. By this point the enemy team is probably able to shatter your shields pretty fast otherwise. If you're still stomping the enemy team for the most part, feel free to keep stacking damage items instead, it's just by this point in the game your teammates' builds are usually fully online and able to pick up the slack on DPS.",
